# CeeLing fact pack: project-specific shim functions that still live INSIDE the compiler.
# Migrated 2026-11-02 from library_summary.cpp's isKnownQualifiedFreeFunction, no change in behaviour.
#
# These belong to imgui-cling (a hand-written, UNCHECKED C++ glue shim, imgui-cling/shim/gfx_shim.{h,cpp}, wrapping
# GLFW + OpenGL behind plain-primitives-only free functions: no pointers, no callbacks, no object types cross the
# boundary, so no ownership or borrow question reaches CeeLing's analysis). They should move into that project as
# its own pack (or `ext_fn` declarations) so the compiler carries no project names: TODO.md, third-party facts.
# The check is a bare string match on the called name, whether or not a namespace qualifier is present.
# `gfx_get_mouse_pos` is NOT here: it takes float* out-params, so it stays C++-internal.
@pack shims-imgui-cling
@version 1
@origin hand-written, migrated from library_summary.cpp

function gfx_init source=declared review=hand
function gfx_should_close source=declared review=hand
function gfx_begin_frame source=declared review=hand
function gfx_draw_triangle source=declared review=hand
function gfx_end_frame source=declared review=hand
function gfx_shutdown source=declared review=hand
function gfx_draw_rect source=declared review=hand
function gfx_mouse_x source=declared review=hand
function gfx_mouse_y source=declared review=hand
function gfx_mouse_down source=declared review=hand
function gfx_draw_text source=declared review=hand
function gfx_text_width source=declared review=hand
function gfx_float_to_string source=declared review=hand
